{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.bridge_joins_consecutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.bridge_joins_consecutive","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/StrandLayoutForcesChain.lean#L89-L93","doc":"And it joins nucleon `k` to nucleon `k+1`, which is what makes the wired bond set\nthe chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.bridge_crosses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.bridge_crosses","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/StrandLayoutForcesChain.lean#L82-L87","doc":"The bridge generator the producer actually uses for the `k`-th bond, `3k+2`,\ndoes cross a boundary — the positive direction of `crossesBlocks_iff`, instantiated\nat the measured value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.no_single_generator_joins_nonadjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.no_single_generator_joins_nonadjacent","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/StrandLayoutForcesChain.lean#L73-L80","doc":"**No single generator joins non-adjacent nucleons**, at any `A`. So the edges\nexpressible as one crossing are exactly the `A − 1` consecutive pairs, and the\ncomplete graph is not among the bond sets this layout can write. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.adjacent_of_crosses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.adjacent_of_crosses","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/StrandLayoutForcesChain.lean#L66-L71","doc":"**And the two nucleons it joins are consecutive.** This is the half that forces\nthe chain: a boundary-crossing generator never reaches past its neighbour. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.crossesBlocks_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.crossesBlocks_iff","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/StrandLayoutForcesChain.lean#L60-L64","doc":"**A generator crosses a nucleon boundary exactly at `m ≡ 2 (mod 3)`.**\n`σ_m` swaps strands `m` and `m+1`; those lie in different nucleons iff `m % 3 = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain.block","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/StrandLayoutForcesChain.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The nucleon index owning strand `m`, under the framework's layout in which\nnucleon `k` occupies strands `3k`, `3k+1`, `3k+2` of a `3A`-strand braid. ","signatureChunk":0}]}